220
00:13:12,916 --> 00:13:14,136
Oh, shit!

221
00:13:14,136 --> 00:13:29,396
I'll start with the seventh and last car.

222
00:13:29,396 --> 00:13:31,776
All of the world government officials are there.

223
00:13:34,776 --> 00:13:37,796
In order of increasing strength, the fifth car is next.

224
00:13:38,996 --> 00:13:41,976
That car holds 40 Marines and the man who leads them,

225
00:13:42,056 --> 00:13:44,976
a Navy headquarters captain and former knight named T-Bone.

226
00:13:45,416 --> 00:13:47,556
Next in the fourth car, we have Wanzai,

227
00:13:47,836 --> 00:13:50,696
an accomplished martial artist from Cypherpole number seven,

228
00:13:50,936 --> 00:13:53,456
who also happens to be the head steward on this trip.

229
00:13:53,456 --> 00:13:55,636
Standing by in the third car is Nero,

230
00:13:55,956 --> 00:13:59,056
the newest member of CP-9 and a force to be reckoned with.

231
00:13:59,056 --> 00:14:16,396
Anyway, although we are escorting criminals with government personnel

232
00:14:16,396 --> 00:14:18,656
as trained and powerful as the ones I mentioned,

233
00:14:18,656 --> 00:14:21,196
we needn't worry about the possibility of a raid.

234
00:14:21,196 --> 00:14:23,856
Our military might is represented throughout this train.

235
00:14:28,476 --> 00:14:29,756
Straw help!

236
00:14:29,956 --> 00:14:30,516
Nero!

237
00:14:31,596 --> 00:14:33,036
We're here to help!

238
00:14:33,776 --> 00:14:34,696
Come out!

239
00:14:35,016 --> 00:14:36,456
Where are you?

240
00:14:38,256 --> 00:14:41,276
Mr. Foreman, it must be hard for you to even move.

241
00:14:41,436 --> 00:14:42,676
Maybe you should take a little break.

242
00:14:42,696 --> 00:14:44,396
Don't be stupid. This is nothing.

243
00:14:44,576 --> 00:14:45,716
Hurry up and find them.

244
00:14:45,736 --> 00:14:46,276
Yes, sir.

245
00:14:47,756 --> 00:14:50,396
Has anyone gone to bring Iceberg up to speed?

246
00:14:50,396 --> 00:14:52,356
Two men went to give him a report.

247
00:14:59,816 --> 00:15:01,736
Hey, where are you going, Mr. Iceberg?

248
00:15:02,836 --> 00:15:03,316
Sir?

249
00:15:06,116 --> 00:15:07,156
Hey, Zorro!

250
00:15:07,636 --> 00:15:09,016
Where are you?

251
00:15:09,236 --> 00:15:10,936
Answer us, Straw Hat!

252
00:15:12,196 --> 00:15:12,676
Woofie!

253
00:15:13,196 --> 00:15:13,976
Zorro, Woofie!

254
00:15:14,276 --> 00:15:15,576
Come on, guys, answer me!

255
00:15:15,816 --> 00:15:17,016
Where the heck are you?

256
00:15:17,016 --> 00:15:20,336
What's that?

257
00:15:21,196 --> 00:15:21,936
Food, you say?

258
00:15:21,956 --> 00:15:22,776
Yes, that's right.

259
00:15:22,876 --> 00:15:23,556
We need meat.

260
00:15:23,656 --> 00:15:24,776
All the meat you can find.

261
00:15:24,876 --> 00:15:26,476
And hurry, we're running out of time.

262
00:15:28,356 --> 00:15:31,556
How did we end up being a couple of errand boys for that girl?

263
00:15:31,596 --> 00:15:32,676
We're not doing this for her.

264
00:15:32,856 --> 00:15:34,056
We're doing it for Pauly.

265
00:15:34,256 --> 00:15:35,716
He's so devoted to that crazy woman,

266
00:15:35,796 --> 00:15:36,756
